                <pb facs="0285" n="197" xml:id="pg197"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.6374/1175: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Culbertson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-06-28T18:00:00-04:00">June 28, 1933—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 6:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>81. Referring to my telegram No. 80, June 26, 11 a.m., Minister of Finance
                    informed representative of National City Bank that article 30 of the eighth
                    draft would be eliminated. I had indicated to the Minister for Foreign Affairs
                    that the proposed discrimination against American interests could not be
                    accepted.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Culbertson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
